<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 5.046 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 5.046 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 5.046 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and eight repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    356 days   20.35 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days   20.39 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     63 days</p>
<p>    600 million     48 days</p>
<p>    700 million     47 days</p>
<p>    700 million     41 days</p>
<p>    700 million     38 days</p>
<p>    650 million     31 days</p>
<p>    600 million     26 days</p>
<p>    146 million	3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( -- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
